ly cite one","-another. We then read the exact open-stacks search of Chu and Stuckey (2009) as","-a pathwidth algorithm. Two of its published dominance theorems are false; a","-14-vertex graph refutes the first, and the same graph refutes its restatement in","-Chu's thesis. The repaired rule is an instance of Tamaki's commitment lemma and","-costs one bipartite matching per candidate. The whole repaired search is proved","-sound in Lean. Run as the default in both of our solvers, it has re-refuted 112 of","-the 115 corpus values that rested on the published rules, changing none, and it","-emits certificates that an independent checker verifies. The equivalences make one","-certified width an answer to every problem in the exact core, and we release","-17,714 isomorphism classes from twenty benchmark collections, 16,087 with a","-certified pathwidth and a witness layout.","+\\noindent","+The minimization of open stacks problem (MOSP) asks for the order in which to","+make a set of patterns so that the fewest customer orders are open at once.","+\\citet{LY2002} listed twelve problems from operations research, VLSI design and","+graph theory, MOSP among them, as equal to it ``plus or minus one'', and gave","+no proofs. We ask which of these equalities are true, and what follows when","+results, algorithms and benchmarks are moved between the twelve problems","+through pathwidth, the quantity that connects them. We find four things. First,","+eight of the twelve rows are exact, counting pathwidth itself: each equals","+pathwidth or pathwidth plus one. Two lie in bands one and two wide, and two are","+false as stated; every relation is proved, and machine-checked in Lean.","+Second, the literature has settled on the name pathwidth, used more than three","+times as often as the other eleven names together, and the three communities","+rarely cite one another. Third, the best exact algorithm for MOSP, the search of","+\\citet{ChuStuckey2009}, is a pathwidth algorithm, and two of its published","+dominance theorems are false. The correct rule was already known for","+pathwidth; we show that it is tested by one bipartite matching per candidate,","+and prove the repaired search sound. In our implementation it costs at most","+2\\% more search nodes on each benchmark set, and it re-proved all 115 benchmark","+optima that rested on the published rules, changing none. Fourth, we release","+17,714 benchmark graphs, distinct up to isomorphism, from twenty collections,","+16,087 of them with a certified pathwidth and a layout that attains it."," \\end{abstract}"," "," \\input{sec1_intro}"]}]}],"moreFiles":0,"changedFiles":["/home/al/dev/MOSP/paper2/latex/sec1_intro.tex","/home/al/dev/MOSP/paper2/latex/main.tex"]}}}
